Title: Cross-lingual retrieval: query in EN/FR finds Vietnamese content
Created: 2026-08-27
Author: claude

--- log ---
2026-08-27T06:44Z claude created

2026-08-27T06:50Z claude note author-flagged priority; body carries the proposal awaiting ratification

--- body ---
## Context
The library holds Vietnamese-language content; the author queries in English
or French. R7 promises "multilingual by default", but that is each language
working in its own lane: nothing today promises that an English query finds a
Vietnamese document. That is a different property — cross-lingual retrieval.
This ticket formulates the requirement, the constraints, and the design
amendment. The documents are edited only after the author's ruling lands in
DECISIONS.md; until then the proposal lives here.

## Proposed requirement
**R29 — the query language is not the document language.** A query in
English or French retrieves relevant Vietnamese content without the user
translating anything. Testable form: the R21 golden fixture gains a
cross-lingual slice — EN and FR queries whose golden answer sets are
Vietnamese entries — gated separately from the monolingual queries, so a
regression names the promise it broke. And when the semantic path is down
(keyword-only degradation, DESIGN.md §2.7), the reply says cross-language
matching is unavailable instead of returning a silent miss — an R18
extension.

## Constraints the world imposes
- Keyword search cannot cross languages. FTS5/BM25 has no path from
  "hydropower" or "hydroélectricité" to "thủy điện". The embedding space is
  the only cross-lingual channel; the requirement stands or falls on the
  embedder.
- R10 (local by default) rules out translation services on the default path,
  and a local translation model would add weight and latency for one
  language pair. Query translation is out of scope, said out loud.
- Cross-lingual alignment is a property of the embedder's training and
  varies by pair (EN-VI is typically weaker than EN-FR). It must be measured
  on the real library, not read off a model card — starting with verifying
  what upstream's default embedder actually is at HEAD.
- Vietnamese itself already rides the existing machinery: space-separated
  syllables tokenize under unicode61 (no CJK-style n-gram table needed), and
  remove_diacritics 2 folds tone marks — recall-friendly, with a disclosed
  precision cost (tone-stripped syllables collide). Same-language VI keyword
  search is served today; the gap is only cross-lingual.
- The fusion seam: on a cross-lingual query the keyword list is empty or
  noise, so ranking must not require keyword confirmation before a semantic
  hit can surface. This is the frac_vec question ticket 0031 already owns;
  the cross-lingual slice becomes its hardest test case.

## Proposed design (amendments; land only after ratification)
- No new machinery on the query path: cross-lingual retrieval rides the
  semantic path (DESIGN.md §2.6) on the multilingual embedder. What changes
  is that the promise becomes measured and gated instead of assumed.
- New experiment **X8**, on the author's machine (real VI content; substrate
  map in 0025): a pinned set of EN and FR queries with known-relevant VI
  entries; measure recall@10 for the default embedder and one or two local
  alternatives. Rule: the best local model meeting the golden thresholds
  ships as the default; if none does, the promise degrades to a typed
  disclosure (CROSS_LINGUAL_DEGRADED — the CJK posture of §2.6, transposed)
  and any bigger-model opt-in becomes an explicit decision, never silent.
- The golden fixture corpus (0029) gains VI documents and the cross-lingual
  query slice.
- R18's empty-result sentences gain the keyword-only disclosure above.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] Proposal put to the author; the ruling (ratify, amend, or veto) lands
      in DECISIONS.md
- [ ] On ratification: REQUIREMENTS.md gains R29, CONSTRAINTS.md the
      sharpenings, DESIGN.md §2.6/§2.8/§3 the amendments; this body becomes
      pointers
- [ ] X8 and its decision rule recorded in DESIGN.md §3 and in 0025's
      substrate map
- [ ] 0029's scope extended with the cross-lingual slice
- [ ] make check green
